      "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story.\nAsset type: one 3-column × 3-row original illustration atlas for a first-grade Chinese language lesson set around a community storytelling radio show. Each of the nine cells is a standalone square, exactly equal grid positions and full-bleed; every subject stays well within its own cell. No gutter is needed. No text, letters, numbers, marks, captions, typography, brands or watermark. Visual style fine paper texture, matte gouache, clean cut-paper silhouettes, deep pine green and warm cream with apricot and persimmon orange. Child-friendly, quiet uncluttered backgrounds, thumbnail readability. Use wholly original scenes, simple expressive faces.\nRow 1 left: community radio event, two children set a tabletop microphone on a little rounded table near an open picture book, green curtains and warm wall, one child a school-age girl with orange scarf and bobbed dark hair. Row 1 center: at the same storytelling event, an older woman and an older man greet the child and her adult caregivers, everyone at a comfortable distance, welcoming; composition with a few clear faces. Row 1 right: a small open notebook, unlettered calendar with blank pale blocks, a warm orange sunset on one side and fresh green spring buds on the other, visual cues for time, no printed numbers.\nRow 2 left: a garden table with a hand placing a bean seed in a tray, next to a lush plant bearing recognizable long green bean pods; the same kind of bean shown in both, one linked visual idea. Row 2 center: a large leafy tree gives cool shade to two children sitting together reading, a small watering can under the tree as a visual clue someone previously cared for it. Row 2 right: a child beginning to walk along a long simple gently curving path, only one first clear footstep near their shoe, destination small and far, no sign or letters.\nRow 3 left: a child is proud of a tidy stack of three handmade wooden blocks and tries adding one more above it, secure hands, improvement through a small next action. Row 3 center: quiet indoor picture exhibition, two friends close together speaking softly, a third nearby person studies pictures on a wall. Row 3 right: bright simple practice hall, a child standing by a microphone speaks to three seated classmates several meters away, the listeners look toward the speaker, room layout shows distance, no text and no sound waves drawn.\nUse natural poses and no extra distracting objects. The requested palette and illustrative style must be shared by all cells."
