      "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story.\nAsset type: one 3×3 transparent sprite atlas with 9 isolated paper-cut illustrations for a first-grade Chinese lesson. True alpha background and empty space around every subject. Divide into exactly 3 columns and 3 rows, equal cell boundaries. Center each object within its own cell and keep it to about 60% of the cell. No gridlines, text, numbers, labels or added icons. Same matte gouache, fine paper grain, deep pine green, warm cream, apricot and orange color palette. Clean simple contours for recognition in thumbnails.\nRow 1 left: portrait from the shoulders up of a friendly 6-year-old girl with a short dark bob and an orange scarf. Row 1 center: portrait from the shoulders up of an adult woman with a dark bun and a cream and warm orange scarf. Row 1 right: portrait from the shoulders up of an adult man with short dark hair and a pine-green cardigan. Only one portrait per cell.\nRow 2 left: portrait from the shoulders up of a silver-haired older woman smiling, round glasses and muted apricot clothes. Row 2 center: portrait from the shoulders up of a silver-haired older man smiling, warm brown cardigan. Row 2 right: a small toy delivery cart seen in 2D side view with the hood pointing to the RIGHT, two visible dark wheels, pine-green body, orange front light.\nRow 3 left: identical toy cart, same orientation, a small light-orange glow right at the hood to indicate animation; no detached trail. Row 3 center: one simple warm yellow five-point wooden star token with a tiny orange circle at its center, no text, suitable as identical marker on a direction map. Row 3 right: an entire little green cardboard reference figure seen from above, body aligned vertically, FACE and small triangular orange direction pointer oriented toward the TOP of the cell, use big simple shape and clear contrast. This figure will be rotated by code.\nKeep the 9 cutouts self-contained. No cast shadows or background fill."
